03:25.180 --> 03:26.910
Stop it, Kaidoh.

03:26.910 --> 03:28.330
{ambient: split here}No violence.

03:29.190 --> 03:30.140
He's not worth punching anyway. {alternatively: hariai- competition / rivalry}

03:30.140 --> 03:33.100
Echizen, seriously?

03:33.470 --> 03:35.170
Loss of memory...

03:38.590 --> 03:40.940
That's just excellent. {erai=excellent / terrible http://tangorin.com/words/erai}{Unless you wan't to make him sound sarcastic, use: That's just excellent.}

03:41.900 --> 03:44.310
<i>What happened at Karuizawa?</i>

03:49.110 --> 03:50.450
It can't be helped.

03:50.450 --> 03:52.950
For now, let's just concentrate on the next match.

03:52.950 --> 03:54.090
That's right.

03:54.090 --> 03:57.000
By watching a match, he may just recall things.

03:59.340 --> 04:02.930
<b>The second match of the 
National Tournament Finals will now begin.</b>

04:02.930 --> 04:06.890
<b>Seishun Gakuen Doubles 2: Inui and Kaidoh pair versus...</b>

04:06.890 --> 04:10.810
<b>Rikkaidai Fuzoku Doubles 2: Yanagi and Kirihara pair.</b>

04:17.660 --> 04:21.570
Against such guys, 15 minutes will be enough. { Just 15 minutes with such guys is sufficient.}

04:22.390 --> 04:23.490
We'll crush you. {or: I'll crush you.}

04:27.600 --> 04:29.490
Is this destiny as well?

04:29.490 --> 04:31.950
{ambient: split here}To be fighting you again... {...be fighting against you again.}

04:33.050 --> 04:33.980
Yes.

04:40.580 --> 04:41.960
They are strong.

04:41.960 --> 04:45.570
Much stronger than any doubles pair we've competed with before.

04:45.570 --> 04:47.140
