<i>Impossible.</i>

12:22.260 --> 12:26.930
Against a ball with a spin, I'll just apply more spin in the opposite direction.

12:26.930 --> 12:29.720
This must be when a schemer drowns in his own plan.

12:29.720 --> 12:30.930
<i>Impossible.</i>

12:30.930 --> 12:33.770
<i>{ambient: split here}If even this data is ineffective, then...</i>

12:34.890 --> 12:40.320
In order to return the trap, he pretended to be trapped by the opponent's tactics.

12:40.320 --> 12:44.790
With this, the opponent receives greater emotional damage.

12:44.790 --> 12:48.280
Still, our officer sure is scary.{this sanbō 【参謀】= staff officer}

12:55.540 --> 12:57.950
Forgive me for this, Sadaharu. {Pardon me, Sadaharu}{I used this kanben 【勘弁】=pardon/ forgive; or you prefer this kanben 【簡便】=handy/ simple and easy}

13:03.640 --> 13:04.920
15-0.

13:04.920 --> 13:08.140
I can read all of your thoughts precisely. {...thoughts accurately.}

13:17.840 --> 13:19.020
30-0.

13:26.530 --> 13:28.870
Will Inui-senpai be fine?

13:28.870 --> 13:30.450
At this rate, we'll lose.

13:30.450 --> 13:33.530
Inui's heart has completely sunk. {...completely sunk./ given up}

13:33.530 --> 13:35.370
He's crashed. {http://tangorin.com/words/ochiru}

13:38.920 --> 13:39.750
Utsusemi.{Cicada} {Please confirm if he said cicada}{TL Note: Utsusemi means "Cicada."}

13:43.420 --> 13:45.530
Game, Rikkaidai Fuzoku.

13:45.530 --> 13:47.380
5-0. {ambient: timing needs adjustment}

