19:52.270 --> 19:53.500
Inui-senpai.

19:55.950 --> 19:57.160
It can't be!

19:57.160 --> 20:00.550
{ambient: split here}He actually gathered data in that condition?

20:01.790 --> 20:02.630
Let's do... our doubles.

20:02.630 --> 20:04.520
{ambient: split here}Let's do... our doubles.

20:04.520 --> 20:05.010
Yes!

20:07.950 --> 20:10.130
All right, Inui-senpai!

20:10.130 --> 20:12.100
From here on, the real counter-attack starts!

20:20.910 --> 20:22.580
Inui-senpai. Inui-senpai!

20:22.580 --> 20:23.780
Inui-senpai. Inui-senpai!

20:24.320 --> 20:26.700
That was splendid, Sadaharu. {Well done, Sadaharu.}

20:36.000 --> 20:38.960
<b>Due to the retirement of Seishun Gakuen's Inui and Kaidoh pair,</b>

20:38.960 --> 20:42.510
<b>the winners are Rikkaidai Fuzoku's Yanagi and Kirihara pair.</b>

22:11.440 --> 22:13.030
